%I A008840 #35 Oct 18 2026 23:08:16
%S A008840 0,1,1,2,3,7,30,716,6001501
%N A008840 Number of monotone self-dual Boolean functions of n variables that are inequivalent under the symmetric group.
%D A008840 D. E. Knuth, The Art of Computer Programming, Vol. 4A, Section 7.1.1, p. 79.
%H A008840 Daniel Elliott Loeb, <a href="http://www.labri.u-bordeaux.fr/~loeb">Home page</a>
%H A008840 Bartłomiej Pawelski, <a href="https://bip.ug.edu.pl/st-tyt_nauk/117481/bartlomiej_pawelski">Counting and generating monotone Boolean functions</a>, Doctoral Diss., Univ. Gdańsk, (Poland, 2024). See pp. 12, 15, 58, 67, 73. (Abstract in Polish.)
%H A008840 <a href="/index/Bo#Boolean">Index entries for sequences related to Boolean functions</a>
%F A008840 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} A107765(k): a self-dual monotone function of n variables depends on exactly k of them for some k (constants are not self-dual), and up to permutation it is determined by the class of its restriction to those k variables. - _James Guillochon_, Sep 27 2026
%Y A008840 Cf. A003180, A057132, A108803.
%Y A008840 First differences give A107765.
%K A008840 nonn,hard,nice,more,changed
%O A008840 0,4
%A A008840 _Daniel E. Loeb_
%E A008840 a(8) from Bartłomiej Pawelski's thesis (with Andrzej Szepietowski) added by _James Guillochon_, Sep 27 2026
